  message: "Fixed in PR #2198. Re-ran the item's fixture: A.B(), A.B().go(), b = A.B(); b.go(), A.B.C().deep() and the same from an importing file now bind the nested class (instantiates) and its method (calls); on the fixture calls to stand-ins went 10 -> 5 and instantiates 0 -> 5. A dotted name is walked from its root, one member at a time, with no last-segment fallback. pretix: no edge went from an in-repo target to a stand-in; dead-code unchanged (15,324 / 6,052 / 7,660). LEFT, each in the forms table of the package report: cls.B(), self.B().go(), an inherited member reached through a nested class when a twin class name exists, a parameter annotated A.B."  # e1c1
